cation.json"} {"question" "q-162652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-2)$ is $s\\in (2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $1-s$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${s}^{2}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/91b196d5e312c4242a493f65abad556aa7f689640b09e0c51bc9124681abb48a.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in (2,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8cacf0e1948298e0eb7454030623b73f5e4f7dded78ab2c4610490107f291e5" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162652" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0