ha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162652" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "s\\in (2,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+({t}^{3}+1)\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n2t=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{3}+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8cacf0e1948298e0eb7454030623b73f5e4f7dded78ab2c4610490107f291e5" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi n"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi n}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "n\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)={e}^{1-t}\\,i+(2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1)\\,j+t\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component ${e}^{1-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/state.json" "file_sha256" "3904bf5aa136c2350759b4bbf662ea0b27bc705c580f0d92b5bd5d2096856886" "basis" 1239 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162635" "field" nil "attribute" "